 out  but jewel wrote that he was most touched  by a young woman who finally spoke up  and said that she had read the ending of  Mark by herself the night before and  said I cried the tomb is empty but the  only response we see and Mark is fear  mark is relentlessly consistent Jesus's  disciples are not miraculously  transformed by an empty tomb into heroes  or saints any more than some of us will  be after this service even when the  promised resurrection comes they run  away in terror they have failed Jesus at  every step along the way and even now  when everything he predicted has come  true they are stunned and frightened  they are not ready the routes a mark  story Jesus has told the disciples not  to tell anyone about him who he is or  the miracles he performs and now finally  at the end of the story the young man in  white in the tomb says go and tell  finally go and tell and what do they do  they run away and they don't tell  anybody I've told many of you an old  family legend of mine that I think fits  with this feeling about Mark from San  Sabbath street in El Paso Texas where I  grew up I must have been for when this  happened because I think we moved out of  that house when I was five some of you  know my father worked for a drugstore  chain they still existed at that time  and one of the joys of being his son was  that Easter candy was dropped off in his  office by the salesman and came home to  me and my brother  the most glorious of which was every  year the giant solid chocolate Easter  rabbit for a four-year-old you can  imagine this was more pleasure than I  could handle on Saturday morning before  Easter my father arrived home from work  about noon and in his usual wonderful  soft-spoken way presented my older  brother and I with our rabbits this was  a moment to be savored literally and  emotionally we retired to our shared  bedroom and carefully unwrapped our  prizes pure brown delight with pink  icing eyes and finally when we could no  wait no 