rance to the disciples that it  will all be all right mark sends us home  from easter worship not with the sense  that the story of jesus is neatly  wrapped up for another year sending us  home inspired but perhaps unable to  recognize that idealized story in the  lives we go home to mark sends us home  to our real lives lives with daily  struggles to care for the ones we love  to figure out who we are and where we're  going and what is right to learn what it  means to do justice and love kindness  and walk humbly in a world that perverts  justice and loves violence and walks  telling god what to do mark opens a door  yes the disciples did fail every step  along the way right up to the end just  as we do but Jesus does not fail them  and that's what matters the young men in  white in the tomb says a few simple  words he says do not be alarmed you are  looking for Jesus who was crucified he  has been raised he is not here look  there is the place they laid him but go  tell his disciples and Peter that he is  going ahead of you to Galilee and there  you will see him just as he told you the  message of marks Easter is he is going  head of you whether the frightened women  tell anyone or not Jesus is already on  the way to Galilee he's not lingering in  the graveyard to reassure us but as  always he is out ahead of us fulfilling  his promises to us loose in the world  marks Easter is not a wax imitation as  long as Easter is about resolving the  story with the happy ending we desire we  can close Holy Week reassured that God  is in God's heaven and all is well with  the world but marks Jesus isn't at least  bit interested in our reassurance even  our response is not the issue Jesus does  not wait for us to get the concept he is  off to heal the broken and share the  good news of God with the poor he has  defeated death he has opened the gates  of hell however you define it he has  proven that love can defeat power and  weakness defeat strength he has showed  us that the